{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type","id":877300,"title":"For the 'other shifters' which is your fave type?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-28T21:12:45-07:00","id":877300,"title":"For the 'other shifters' which is your fave type?","content":"Of all the other shifters, i have always loved Gurahl the bear folk. Mokole pull in a 2nd place for me, while Bastet hold third.. Never really been interested in the Nuwisha or Corax, and never had a DM willing to allow anyone to take Annassi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T00:14:43-07:00","id":877416,"title":"","content":"For me it's probably the Mokole followed by the Gurahl, with me just not really caring for or about the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1069-archmage-joda","name":"Archmage Joda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T00:59:45-07:00","id":877446,"title":"","content":"Corax are probably my only favorites. The Nagah and Ananasi are distant ties for 2nd, and Mokole and Ratkin tied at a 4th after that.<br /> <br /> The Bastet, Nuwisha, and Kitsune esp. are low on my list partially because they never feel &quot;unique&quot; enough for me. The Bastet's biggest difference from the Garou is that they're more prone to being loners and secretive... which is pretty shit for play. The Nuwisha are basically playing an all Wendigo/Uktena Ragabash game, and the Kitsune feel more like they're a Japanese offshoot of the Uktena (with the focus on mystic powers) than a separate Fera. The last two are also things that could be folded into the Garou to make the Garou more global and cohesive by having more species than just wolves associated with them.<br /> <br /> The Rokea, and Gurahl are neat concepts, but they developed them too much towards being NPCs than PCs this makes them extremely difficult to actually play; which is a big down side for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T09:22:35-07:00","id":877787,"title":"","content":"Definitely the Mokole. The sheer number of differences you can have make them incredibly interesting to build a character with. From a lore perspective, I would probably still stick with them, as the Mnesis I think is an interesting concept on par with being able to do an Umbral quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T09:45:46-07:00","id":877817,"title":"","content":"Gurahl and Nuwisha, because I love the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Anasasi and Corax, because I think their various forms are bad ass.<br /> <br /> Anasasi are probably the most interesting to me, but Gurahl are definitely more easily played as a PC.<br /> <br /> <br /> Never had a ST willing to allow me to play any of the four, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T09:51:18-07:00","id":877822,"title":"","content":"Mokole and Kitsune. Corax are not bad either.<br /> <br /> And that is my substantive contribution to the conversation. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T12:08:43-07:00","id":877960,"title":"","content":"Nagah the sheer Angst, and the fact Garou likely... wouldnt appreciate the Nagah's purpose, yet the Nagah wish to see the Garou suceed as a whole, makes them VERY appealing to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T12:43:13-07:00","id":877991,"title":"","content":"Corax seem to be the most fun to me in terms of variety of play and variety of plots, and how easily you can drop them into just about any situation. If other fera are rare (as far as the Garou are concerned) in your setting, like they were originally written...not sure how it's changed over the editions, it can be hard to explain why there's Gurahl around that nobody knew about, and Nagah etc are totally out of the question in most situations. Bastet are so well developed culturally that it almost seems weird to put them in a Werewolf campaign, but it's hard to do a group of just Bastet. On the other hand Corax-outta-nowhere is always believable.<br /> <br /> I like Nuwisha in theory. They're fun to read stories about. They're much harder to play; I don't think I fit those pants nearly as well as I wish I did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T12:46:42-07:00","id":877996,"title":"","content":"The fact that I can build a &quot;dragon&quot; as a Mokole makes them a very close second-favorite, but the Anansi are just all kinds of cool, especially with crawlerling form. So they're my favorites. I like them better than the werewolves, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:02:59-07:00","id":878133,"title":"","content":"I've always had fun using the Corax, having them roll into a caern talking a mile a minute and maybe or maybe not have something useful to contribute at the moment. It may be due to the first game I set up the caern totem was Raven so the local Garou had an established place for Corax to stay and they're were almost always at least one Corax taking advantage of the Garou's hospitality. The Corax were always an easy way to drop a story hook in a pinch and an interesting way to alter usual Garou battle planning, having air support nearby all the time.<br /> <br /> My other to favorites were are probably the Gurahl and Nuwisha. The Gurahl as master lore keepers in hidden groves of Gaia hidden in the deep wilderness has always seemed like a good way to give the Garou a quest for information only this sage would know. The Nuwisha also showed up every now and then to give the Garou a horrible headache, like keeping the sept on it's toes by booby-trapping the sept's territory and leading the Garou on a goose chase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:14:24-07:00","id":878153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archmage Joda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=877416#post877416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it's probably the Mokole followed by the Gurahl, with me just not really caring for or about the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of the Gator folk's 4 subtypes, which is your fave?? I toss between Zhong lung and regular ole mokole-Mbembe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=877817#post877817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never had a ST willing to allow me to play any of the four, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That bites. I have often had luck getting ST's to allow one 'off the norm&quot;..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:21:31-07:00","id":878160,"title":"","content":"Rokea and Mokole sold me on W:tA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T17:25:16-07:00","id":878257,"title":"","content":"I like the Ajaba but my favorite are the Nuwisha.<br /> I rarely play as a character but when I do I want to play something fun. That's why I like to play Ti-Malice Neil Winterhold IRS auditor. &quot;Yes, I have an appointment I'm here to review the corporate tax statements for 2014-2015.&quot; &quot;Yes here is my identification and just for my notes what was your name?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T18:12:39-07:00","id":878290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=878153#post878153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of the Gator folk's 4 subtypes, which is your fave?? I toss between Zhong lung and regular ole mokole-Mbembe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm partial to the good ol mokole-mbembe myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1069-archmage-joda","name":"Archmage Joda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:42:16-07:00","id":878403,"title":"","content":"That does seem to be common. the Indian ones and the Australian ones are the 2 least used i find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T09:46:04-07:00","id":879568,"title":"","content":"Mokole- For too many different reasons. <br /> 1) I'm an a herper by hobby (Currently own 17 different herps and that's not counting my dart frog tadpoles). To be able to play as a werereptile was a big plus for me, so I was excited to buy both the Mokole and Nagah breed books. The only thing that takes the Nagah from being tied with the dragons is that I can't find anyone who wants to play an all Nagah game and well they don't mix well. W20 giving us the Ao was what took it over the top for me (big time turtle guy)<br /> 2) Archid form- you can base entire concepts around this form. For me building the archid isn't all about more power, but to have it be a reflection of the character's persona. I have a shinning for example that I have turn into a large bipedal chameleon for example. Color change rotating eyes and a long tongue don't exactly make one a battle tank, but fun none the less. The customization here threw the Mokole instantly to the top slot.<br /> 3) Culture- I have been a big fan of a lot of the cultural stuff written about the mokole. Considering their kin the &quot;8th sun&quot; to me always made me read that they have a close relationship with their kin and see them more then just property or breeding stock but vital members of the Wallow. I was amused to read in revised Rage Across the World about how Mokole applied to NGO's and the UN for various grants and aide to help different areas of Africa where their kin could be found. The idea that they were thinking outside the typical shifter box amused me.<br /> 4) Purpose- I love the idea of being the memory, and how this could shape your character's out look on life. Mokole can remember being different races/genders/and even changing breeds. It gives them a unique in site into the world. I also think gifts like &quot;Walk Into My Eyes&quot; and &quot;View the Seed&quot; are interesting and can be fun to use in game, along with rites like &quot;Burn the Library&quot; and &quot;Silence of the Oracles&quot; can not only be useful but can really open the door for a lot of fun role playing. I think its a shame that the Mokole didn't get more gifts and rites along these lines then what they did, like maybe an ability like lvl 3 Auspex or lvl 3 Mytherceria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T22:38:41-07:00","id":879922,"title":"","content":"I cant say I have read all the tribe-books and am well informed on all the tribes but so far my favourite are the Ananasi, probably followed by the Nagah<br /> <br /> I actually do play an Ananasi right now (see other thread) and I just love the different outlook on things when compared to the other breeds and also the alien-ness of the spider-shifters. They also have quite a lot of very interesting abilities and gifts. Yes even if you don't go for the most efficient ones for fighting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Its interesting how they see it as their duty to restore balance to the Triad, to even possibly get rid of the Weaver so that Ananasa can take her place (and do what she was made to do) even though Ananasa is held prisoner by the Wyrm yet they still seem to think she is totally uninfluenced by him and totally tricking him by being in contact with her children without him noticing.<br /> I also like all the options for subterfuge and stealth you can get.<br /> This time around I opted to not boost any abilities at character creation but instead put lots of freebies in merits and stuff like that that I wouldn't be able to learn later in the game. It gives me even more basic abilities to play with and helps explain the continued survival of the character in the time before the game started.<br /> <br /> I'm not even a great fan of spiders in real life. Actually I guess I even have a mild case of Arachnophobia (though much less severe than several other people I know, maybe it shouldn't be called that at all in my case, don't know) but on the other hand I still find them very interesting animals nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Had to decide between Ananasi and Nagah for the current game. As its a Hengeyokai based game a Nagah would have been somewhat easier to include but would have brought with it a lot of other difficulties. Like having to be reeeeeaaaaally careful about not letting any outsider know that you're a Nagah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T00:53:39-07:00","id":879963,"title":"","content":"You sound like one of the guys i gamed with in Cornwall in the UK. A big arachnophobe, but he loved Ananasi..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T01:39:26-07:00","id":879986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=879963#post879963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You sound like one of the guys i gamed with in Cornwall in the UK. A big arachnophobe, but he loved Ananasi..</div> </div> </div> </div>nah, I'm not really a BIG arachnophobe. I don't really like them and I wouldn't get a pet spider or anything like that but I do find them interesting from a.... hmm..... maybe &quot;scientific&quot; point of view. Also I do have a liking of somewhat strange and alien things in fantasy backgrounds so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11694,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","user":"Hexer","date":". 05-02-2016, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T05:19:39-07:00","id":880071,"title":"","content":"Conceptually, I think I like all the breeds. However, I do feel the earlier breeds got the shaft because they were just stupidly focused variants of Garou with little to actually give them their own character. Gurahl are all misunderstood CoG. Nuwisha are all Ragabash. Corax were an early attempt at being different, and their concept is cool, but they got shafted with a super short book. The Ajaba even got a little chunk in a book about their biggest enemies. It took the creation of the Ahadi to actually make them worthwhile and raise them from the status of the occasional Villian and punching bag. Mokole are possibly one of the worst offenders because they really, really do try to be special. And then lose a lot of their oomph thanks to a rather poorly written Breed Book. At least if you focus on the cool things (Archid, Sun, Mnesis, the Streams, some of their artifacts, their Metis) you can play up a pretty cool Breed.<br /> <br /> It's a shame the Kitsune didn't get more variety, they kinda ended up as Garou lite thanks to the fact that they got a mini-breedbook, but I did like their mythology and interaction with the Hengeyokai. That reminds me that I never actually read their writeup in the W20 Changing Breeds, and I probably should. I think I am probably the most lenient towards them of the ones who got handed the cliff-notes ball.<br /> <br /> The winners in the Breed pool are the latter maniacs - Ratkin, Ananasi, Nagah and Rokea. They are all quite a bit harder to crossover with anything else, but that's kinda the point - they literally burst with flavour of their own and can carry whole games on their shoulders.<br /> <br /> Ratkin are batshit insane, and their breedbook manages to paint a brilliant image of eschatonic revolutionaries getting ready for the wrong war of the Apocalypse. Every book that makes the Garou perspective positive in comparison has to be downright special. And the Ratkin manage it by being gleeful about all the chaos.<br /> <br /> Ananasi. Ok, I never understood how you get from Grandfather Spider to the great Spider Queen (something I've actually used in my games to create a schism at one point, actually). However, Ananasa is a brilliant idea. All the shifters had their gods in a rather... hands off holding pattern. You got get as the great unifier, as the grand planer and as a comparativley reasonable objective for your games. Then add an utterly alien mindset, and you're faced with a rather interesting group of characters who can be anything from heroes, villians to antagonists. Good, job whoever wrote them, because these guy make sense, even if it's a bit of work to actually integrate them into a game.<br /> <br /> Nagah. You know how I complained about overcrippling specialisation and how it's a poor excuse to make a good breed? Nagah take that concept and own it. With a very broad and colorful look on the snakes in mythology, and a whole complete game mode that's based on playing them and just them, and a deep seated criticism of what they do and what they did. There is room for some amazing interactions and stories there. It's a bit sad that you will probably never get to play them, but it's still a small price for a really enjoyable book. Also, I do feel that this is what the Corax and the Nuwisha could have turned out if someone actually gave them the time and pagecount they deserved.<br /> <br /> Rokea. Oh momma. These guys are simply amazing. They take the whole game and completley reskin it, terming everything in the perceptions of someone who doesn't understand anything beyond the Sea. It introduced the problems of the Rokea, their rudimentarry politics, the acquatic reinterpetation of the Triat and one of the coolest visuals ever - Giant Gaian Kami-Caern whales. These guys are off. Their logic and values are skewed, and they really, really make sense. This and the Ananasi books may actually fight for my two favourite Werewolf supplements.<br /> Bonus points for actually running a Rokea oneshot at sea in the middle of the night on a rocky beach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T03:49:37-07:00","id":880852,"title":"","content":"I'd like rokea a damsite more if they were playable. They're killing macines, Their powers are brokenly powerful, but they're so dumb they might as well get more intellegent through lobotomy and an exceptionally angry ahroun ain't got shit on em. Like a game as a rokea might as well play itself because of all the frenzies. <br /> <br /> <br /> The absolute favourite is the ratkin of course. They're mental as anything. We should change the line to Ratkin: Pandemonium. It's everything you loved about every other line. The politics are bullshit, the fighting is manic, and the investigative scenes are really about deciding how to cause as much damage as possible. <br /> <br /> I don't care for kitsune much. You're basically a toreador. Or a warlock. It's not very changer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:46:02-07:00","id":881132,"title":"","content":"One of my longer gaming friends said of the Ratkin. they should have called it Rats, the anarchy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:19:39-07:00","id":881297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=880852#post880852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like rokea a damsite more if they were playable. They're killing macines, Their powers are brokenly powerful, but they're so dumb they might as well get more intellegent through lobotomy and an exceptionally angry ahroun ain't got shit on em. Like a game as a rokea might as well play itself because of all the frenzies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple fix that we can always argue for in future books: increase the number of successes to frenzy. That, along with shark form stats that make sense and aren't one-size all. Rokea need a fair bit of work in a number of places, still. I wouldn't call their Gifts overpowered, though; the rest of the Changers just get shafted, and could use a boost.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:35:43-07:00","id":881520,"title":"","content":"Bastets. I get geeked out everytime I read the Breed book.<br /> Ratkin<br /> Nagah<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T05:32:03-07:00","id":881681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=881297#post881297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simple fix that we can always argue for in future books: increase the number of successes to frenzy. That, along with shark form stats that make sense and aren't one-size all. Rokea need a fair bit of work in a number of places, still. I wouldn't call their Gifts overpowered, though; the rest of the Changers just get shafted, and could use a boost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> just so you know, with a few rage and the right bite<br /> + four dice if you're unseen<br /> +2 levels of damage<br /> +3 levels of unsoakable damage<br /> Bite difficulty= 2<br /> (doubling your strength is optional)<br /> <br /> Or alternatively<br /> Everything infront of me is sucked into my mouth to never be seen again. (which is level 5, but let's continue) <br /> <br /> Spend a willpower, your lungs are replaced with gills. There's no water around. You die. The end. <br /> <br /> That said, I do think <i>honesty is the best policy</i> to be the greatest gift since <i>Trust me</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:54:55-07:00","id":881786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=881681#post881681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> just so you know, with a few rage and the right bite<br /> + four dice if you're unseen<br /> +2 levels of damage<br /> +3 levels of unsoakable damage<br /> Bite difficulty= 2<br /> (doubling your strength is optional)<br /> <br /> Or alternatively<br /> Everything infront of me is sucked into my mouth to never be seen again. (which is level 5, but let's continue)<br /> <br /> Spend a willpower, your lungs are replaced with gills. There's no water around. You die. The end.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think <i>honesty is the best policy</i> to be the greatest gift since <i>Trust me</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do know. I also think that Gifts for other character types should have more oomph. Shiva's Might, for example, was intensely disappointing, since even Might of Thor got rid of its weakness phase, and it doesn't compare favorably to Leviathan in this regard. It at least shouldn't inflict a sudden slumber on the character using it. Master of Fire should probably not have a cost, unless you want the cost to come with an increase in effectiveness, etc.<br /> <br /> (Also there are a lot of terrible, terrible countermeasures against bites. Fomori have lots of them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:52:54-07:00","id":881922,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, I'm somewhat surprised that they don't have resist toxin in there, though that'd completely have all ignore the balefire sharks. <br /> <br /> While formori can have something as extreme as xenomorph blood or parasites that eat your entrails they first explode; In The usual fights and breed versus breed fights sharks massively outstomp everything, even garou. Even gurahl for that matter. Difficulty 2 to hit is ridiculous. Ridiculous!!! You combine the stuff about them smashing through walls and flying and you wonder how the wyrm was ever a problem! <br /> <br /> (also, having being a victim of Fenrir's bite, I have to say I'm not a fan of having my massive multi-gift soak pool ignored for a guaranteed three agravated damage. Fortunately it was a light spar for two get of fenrir) <br /> <br /> I'm all for the other breeds to get more gifts, and I understand the Rokea's roll as... Defenders of Sea? Sea's warriors? Gaia's Destroyers? Storyteller's punishment? <br /> It's just I think Rokea should be managable and... well, Not likely to kill your Athro badass in one move, difficulty 2. There's no honourable way to beat someone like that. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:52:44-07:00","id":882347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=881922#post881922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yeah, I'm somewhat surprised that they don't have resist toxin in there, though that'd completely have all ignore the balefire sharks.<br /> <br /> While formori can have something as extreme as xenomorph blood or parasites that eat your entrails they first explode; In The usual fights and breed versus breed fights sharks massively outstomp everything, even garou. Even gurahl for that matter. Difficulty 2 to hit is ridiculous. Ridiculous!!! You combine the stuff about them smashing through walls and flying and you wonder how the wyrm was ever a problem!</div> </div> </div> </div>Because most Kunspawn are on a much longer advancement schedule than Garou. They are naturally unaging, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (also, having being a victim of Fenrir's bite, I have to say I'm not a fan of having my massive multi-gift soak pool ignored for a guaranteed three agravated damage. Fortunately it was a light spar for two get of fenrir)<br /> <br /> I'm all for the other breeds to get more gifts, and I understand the Rokea's roll as... Defenders of Sea? Sea's warriors? Gaia's Destroyers? Storyteller's punishment?<br /> It's just I think Rokea should be managable and... well, Not likely to kill your Athro badass in one move, difficulty 2. There's no honourable way to beat someone like that. </div> </div> </div>Rokea are meant to be Gaia's Eternal Spawn. They have one over on time and entropy, because they can survive literally forever for some alien purpose Gaia only knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:01:01-07:00","id":882354,"title":"","content":"Honestly though their backstory makes me think that it isn't just appearance that is capped at 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:07:52-07:00","id":882357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=882354#post882354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly though their backstory makes me think that it isn't just appearance that is capped at 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fenrir who live in glass houses with the Swords of Heimdall shouldn't throw stones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T18:52:54-07:00","id":882420,"title":"","content":"I liked the Bastet for one big reason - there are many people who do not live in lands that have wolves. Their shapechanging legends include other predators, and most of them tend to be the big cats.<br /> <br /> So if someone really wanted to play this game of savage horror, and if they really wanted to play a character who was African, Indian, or born south of the United States, the thing the makes the best sense is for them to play a wereleopard, weretiger, or werejaguar. Not to somehow figure out how they got this wolfish blood in them and then make them Uktena. It made the game more inclusive. They had that Uktena multiracial option if they did want to play a werewolf. But I can imagine a lot of would be players wanting something more appropriate for that heritage.<br /> <br /> Many of the other breeds seem more fantasy inspired than taken from real folklore, so they didn't have any of that benefit. Often, the backstory worked against how they were actually developed. The Gurahl were supposed to be almost dead except for a few ultra-rare lineages mainly among the animal breed. The Tribebook though mainly showed them from a homid dominated perspective, even the supposed ursine character examples in the back seemed to be homid! The attempt to make them more &quot;playable&quot; subverted how they actually fit into the setting.<br /> <br /> This is coming mostly from an ST perspective, as for the most part I've never been interested in playing any of them as a PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T19:15:32-07:00","id":882436,"title":"","content":"Funny thing is my Get of fenrir was<br /> -Female<br /> -Lupus<br /> -Half black. <br /> -Shows signs of African-Fera ancestry (nothing much. Just a spotted fur pattern. I learnt that the uktena took in fera kinfolk from african slaves, so I didn't think it a bad idea. That, and a strong mate is a strong mate) <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, I took swords of heimdall as a camp enmity. And also, the tribe as a whole looks down on them. The fenrir ideology is a simple one with no care for race or gender... that's a human cultural influence. I really like the get, and I rollplayed my disdain for weakness, especially among the garou, quite well. Like yeah my storyteller was telling me that the get are super racist, but he also thinks blood bonds are unethical. How are blood bonds unethical? They love me. They consent! True love is worth it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T01:34:02-07:00","id":882677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=882420#post882420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the Bastet for one big reason - there are many people who do not live in lands that have wolves. Their shapechanging legends include other predators, and most of them tend to be the big cats.<br /> <br /> So if someone really wanted to play this game of savage horror, and if they really wanted to play a character who was African, Indian, or born south of the United States, the thing the makes the best sense is for them to play a wereleopard, weretiger, or werejaguar. Not to somehow figure out how they got this wolfish blood in them and then make them Uktena. It made the game more inclusive. They had that Uktena multiracial option if they did want to play a werewolf. But I can imagine a lot of would be players wanting something more appropriate for that heritage.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9f/Wolf_distr.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> You know, most RPG markets were pretty much covered by this. South America and Australia even has the benefit of importing all european cultural tropes and mythology. North Africa even had ver y similar myths with Jackals who ahppen to be cousins to wolves. And while your concept is rather inclusive and modern, it does pay to remember that when the WoD was designed the concepts of inclucsivity and multiculturality were in their earliest days. Saying that WW's research was bad and American-centric in the early days is an understatement.<br /> <br /> Sadly, this disqualifies the Bastet book, even if the cat shifters are a deeply intriguing concept. They just gave them too little space and never properly invested into making them different. The authors never got beyond the fact they really thought (household) cats were cool, and making all the cats in the world cool, sneaky, sexy loners. The Bastet as a concept deserve a whole hardcover of their own, and with time they have gained depth (especially the Khan, Bagheera, Simba and Swara), but they really could use facelift with better cultural research and tighter conceptual tasking for them as a Breed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 05-05-2016, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:18:33-07:00","id":883096,"title":"","content":"Ratkin all the way. I love the frothing madness, the freak aspects, the desire to burn it all down and their propensity for falling into epic frenzies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1456-zeke-hubris","name":"Zeke Hubris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:43:20-07:00","id":889198,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately my faves don't lend themselves to mixed games: Nuwisha and Nagah.<br /> <br /> Nuwisha: I love the concept of the Umbra and the trickster ethos. A Nuwisha game, which would necessarily be a solo game, or maybe a game involving a Corax, mage, or changeling pooka (who could conceivably&quot;hang&quot; with a Nuwisha's umbral-ness) just seems like it would make for a solid, deep treatment of umbral adventuring and daring-do.<br /> <br /> Nagah: I love spy fiction and spy drama and spy everything. A Nagah game is basically what happens when you take that genre and mix in a changing breed. You could even modulate from a more action-oriented setting like <i>La Femme Nikita </i>(the original film, or even 90's USA series) to a more paced, paranoia-laden setting reminiscent of <i>Tinker, Tailor, Solider, Spy</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T13:34:15-07:00","id":889326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=889198#post889198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately my faves don't lend themselves to mixed games: Nuwisha and Nagah.<br /> <br /> Nagah: I love spy fiction and spy drama and spy everything. A Nagah game is basically what happens when you take that genre and mix in a changing breed. You could even modulate from a more action-oriented setting like <i>La Femme Nikita </i>(the original film, or even 90's USA series) to a more paced, paranoia-laden setting reminiscent of <i>Tinker, Tailor, Solider, Spy</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Nagah are more spy fiction crossed with a shifter than anything else. Especially with their whole &quot;Don't let anyone know we exist, even our fellow Fera&quot; Rules..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T05:21:00-07:00","id":889801,"title":"","content":"My Top two of the Other Changing Breeds are the Corax and the Rokea.<br /> <br /> I love their litany, I love their views and ways and I love that their war form is embarrassing and ridiculous and further shows how their role is to get info to others to act on that which needs doing.<br /> <br /> The Kunspawn are Magnificent. I hold out for the day that I can convince others to do Rokea game. As I think their simplistic savagery could be portrayed beautifully tragic and darkly mysterious when dealing with Sea and all things of her and those beyond her.<br /> <br /> Next up Mokole. Though I dont run them in games anymore because all any wants is a dragon or godzilla-esque t-rex to rampage with. <br /> <br /> I used to love the Gurahl, now I'm more 'meh' about them.<br /> <br /> Anan..Ananan...Annannan...Werespiders. There is something about how alien they can be along with their total allegiance to the Queen that terrifies and wonders me and I really like it.<br /> <br /> Bastet I dont care about, at all. <br /> <br /> Nuwisha, yawn.<br /> <br /> Ratkin, nope.<br /> <br /> Nagah...*shrug*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T12:35:55-07:00","id":890088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=889801#post889801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next up Mokole. Though I dont run them in games anymore because all any wants is a dragon or godzilla-esque t-rex to rampage with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of my best played Mokole went with <b>pterodactyl</b> type archid forms..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T14:34:39-07:00","id":890178,"title":"","content":"Had a ton of fun with an overgrown chameleon, and a dragon turtle in the past. Never was one for the huge size traits because I always felt they weren't thought out well enough (this has been mentioned on the forums before, that the system doesn't truly reflect the mass gained in strength)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T16:17:37-07:00","id":890226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=890178#post890178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had a ton of fun with an overgrown chameleon, and a dragon turtle in the past. Never was one for the huge size traits because I always felt they weren't thought out well enough (this has been mentioned on the forums before, that the system doesn't truly reflect the mass gained in strength)</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you use the demolition material from Creedbook&quot; Avenger and rule that their Strength applies directly to structural levels, anyway. Even then, though, the trait consistently confused body slams with ramming attacks and Tall needs a different benefit outright to make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T07:19:09-07:00","id":891716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877300-for-the-other-shifters-which-is-your-fave-type?p=889801#post889801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next up Mokole. Though I dont run them in games anymore because all any wants is a dragon or godzilla-esque t-rex to rampage with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not my Sai Chau. He was a Crocodile God. Long Teeth, Armor, Gills, Poison Sacs, and Sacral Plexus. Every round I bit someone for 4 Agg and healed a Courtier with Dragon's Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}